on youtube there are several creators  with either a big four background  or an mbb background talking about their  experiences but very rarely you really  can see a conversation  where these two perspectives meet and  you can really understand and discuss  what the differences are  between big four companies and mbb  companies  this is exactly what this video is going  to be all about  i partnered with kpi consulted at a big  four company and we both  answered the same questions about our  experiences in coinciding and i trust  that the comparison of these answers  will really help you to understand what  distinguishes  mbb firms from big4 firms welcome  everybody to another coffee break  here on my channel firm learning my name  is heinrich and on my channel i want to  help you  to be successful in the first years of  your career  in this video i'm partnering with kp  from the management consultant channel  i can highly recommend her channel she  has some super  interesting videos on consigting and i  will leave a link to her channel  in the video description so check it out  but now instead of me talking about kp  let's hear from her  thanks henry my name is karjal i am a  strategy and innovation consultant at  deloitte i help my clients to create new  products and services  and i also do have a youtube channel on  consulting helping you get into  consulting  wants to in how do you stand out and  also talking through some of the biases  that we really do face  in consulting really excited for this  video and hopefully can help you  understand if  mbb or big4 is for you and indeed this  video is one of two parts so if you want  to see the second part as well  with other questions from both of our  perspective being answered check out  kp's channel in the video description to  see more but now without further ado  let's jump into the questions  big4 is made up of deloitte kpmg ey  and pwc and in 2019 they made up over 40  percent of consulting revenue worldwide  typically they're much larger than mbb  they're more global than mvp  but they also offer more services than  an mbb over the past few years  their consulting divisions have really  branched out to buy smaller agencies  to do supply chain consulting innovation  consulting proposition design  brand and marketing and so on the other  major difference is that mpb definitely  do charge their clients a little bit  more money  and that means you're typically going to  get a higher salary mbb  versus the big four mbb refers to the  leading  three strategy consulting firms mckinsey  bcg  and bain and strategy consulting firms  is a bit misleading because  these firms do not only do strategy  but probably the more correct term to  call them would be  top management consulting the vast  majority of their business is working  together with the top management of  large clients and trying to help them  solve the problems and  issues at the top of mind of the senior  leaders of the top management of these  companies  most of these companies do not  officially disclose their revenue  figures but as per the wikipedia page  the latest estimate is that mckinsey  does roughly 10 billion dollars in  revenue  bcg sits at around 8 billion and bain  sits  around 5 billion regarding employees  mckinsey and bcg are more or less on a  similar level at around 20  000 whereas bain sits at about 10 000  employees globally my perspective of  course will be biased by my time  at mckinsey and of course there are also  differences among these three firms but  overall also from talking to friends who  worked at these other companies at bcg  or bain  i do believe that they are quite similar  in many ways which is why you can  consider my  answers indicatively right for these  other firms as a way  for me personally it wasn't a big factor  i did my  undergrad in munich at the university of  munich and this is when i applied to  mckinsey for an internship and while  being a good and renowned university for  business in germany  it's a large public university with  thousands of  students attending the business program  every semester but overall yes it is  true that mckinsey likes to hire from  the so called target schools from these  elite universities i met  lots and lots of people at mckinsey who  started at the new  as ivy league or at oxbridge or at the  lse or at any other of these  very renowned universities so for sure  this  will increase your chances of getting  into mbb  and adding to that there might also be  differences in the offices how this is  perceived for instance in the us  the differences among universities are  much more salient  compared to a country like germany so  you can likely expect that  in the u.s the target schools are more  important more relevant than what they  are in germany so overall yes it will  help you but by no means this is a hard  requirement and you can get successfully  into mbb without studying at a target  square  so i studied at imperial college london  and definitely the people who  joined with me they definitely came from  a variety of different universities  honestly in the past  big4 definitely did use to recruit from  these elite schools that henry's  mentioned like oxbridge  ivy league and imperial but diversity is  a big thing for big4 firms today  and they hire from a variety of  universities what they've realized is  that hiring from these universities  brings different viewpoints to the table  for their clients everyone has different  experiences different challenges and  struggles in life  and they can go to a variety of  different universities having a good uni  can definitely help you get screened  okay  but it isn't everything so they look at  education  experiences extracurricular activities  achievements and skills  for anyone thinking that education plays  a massive part in the recruitment  process  i would say go on to linkedin have a  look at where people  have studied at mbb and big4 and you'll  realize that education isn't the end all  yes up or out exists and the underlying  idea is that over time  either you continue advancing to the  next role or at some point if you  fail to advance you will be asked to  leave the firm  though it is not as brutal as it maybe  sounds and the reason is that there's a  very transparent  feedback process at every point in time  you  know where you stand in the process and  in the evaluation if for  any reason your performance will be  started to seen as problematic  there will be many iterations of  feedback that people will give you  people will actively reach out to you to  work together with you to work on your  weak points  to make sure that you meet the bar that  you meet  the requirements for the next level to  really help you as much as possible to  be  successful in the firm that being said  at every level there will be people who  will be asked to leave the firm  if you start at an mbb company you just  need to be aware  that these are the roots of the game  that this is how it works  this being said if this is something  that happens to you  the hr professionals will work together  with you to find you a new job  of course mbb firms have a vast network  and will work together with you to help  you  identify new job opportunities that suit  your needs  yes in many countries big4 definitely  does have an up and out process  but in the uk it's actually very  difficult to get fired  for poor performance we have this asus  code of practice  by law it basically says that you have  to consistently show you're a bad  performer for a firm to fire you  they also need to support you so they  need to give you a few chances and also  put you on a supporting plan  to show that they've tried to improve  your performance so the big four does  have very transparent feedback processes  happens once every quarter where  leadership get together to speak about  you  to understand who you support and  identify how everyone's doing  that means it's also a very structured  promotion process so once every year in  the junior levels you can go for  promotion  even early promotion and you have a  defined set of guidelines that you need  to meet  every grade for you to get promoted so  it's really clear if you want to go for  promotion  you know exactly what you need to do  regarding the project setup what  probably distinguishes  most mbb projects from big4 projects  is the team size and the type of topics  that the consultants will work on it is  no  secret that mbb fees are rather  expensive  and for sure more expensive than your  average big4 firm for these  reasons mbb teams are rather small and  rather work on the most important most  pressing challenges that the company is  facing  a typical mbb team size ranges from two  to four consultants  including the project lead and then one  or two partners  joining the team once or twice a week  and then adding their value in their  perspective this way  this means that from early on you are  one of two  one of three or one of four consultants  and of course by that  you are significant part of the team the  responsibility that you will get early  on from your very first  project will be significant due to the  importance of the topics that mbb  firms work with you will work together  with rather senior executives  often even with board members and will  learn to develop  documents for this audience and present  in front of them as well  this being said mbb firms in the last  years  tried to expand the diversity of their  projects in other directions as well  which is why today you can  find projects in an mbb firm that now  more closely resemble  projects that you would also find in  big4 specifically most mbb  firms today also have different  variations of implementation  type of consulting services this means  that you do not only work  on super strategic super conceptual  projects but you also might find  yourself in a position to really work on  projects that are much closer to an  implementation setting that are really  about  execution and bringing ideas to life  often ideas and then  prior teams before you develop with a  client so from this perspective there  for sure  is an overlap regarding the types of  projects and the team setup  between mbb and big4 though still the  typical mbb project will be different  than the typical big4 project  just like henry's mentioned mbb have  definitely branched out to do  implementation work  but big4 definitely real king when it  comes to breadth of services  we acquire some really cool companies to  strengthen our practices from strategy  technology operations supply chain human  capital as well as brand marketing and  innovation  if you're working on a strategy or brand  project you typically do work in smaller  teams of two to four  you'll end up having a partner who looks  after the relationship with the client  a manager and maybe an analyst or a  consultant on that team  on operations and technology projects  they can be really small  from two to four but they can be massive  to 300  so you need to have a variety of  leadership on there  and work in smaller structures where are  still ensuring there's a big  team so typically they end up being in  work streams and you have smaller teams  within it  but those small teams end up being from  4 to 15 to even 20 sometimes  thank you for watching i really hope  that you took some value out of this  video  if you have any more questions just  leave me a comment below in the comment  section  and i will do my very best to answer  every single one please if you took any  value out of this video please destroy  the like button for the youtube  algorithm and also  subscribe to my channel to see even more  content like this if you want to see  even more from me  hit me up on my instagram my instagram  handle is firm learning  and i also have a mailing list with even  more content you can find a sign up link  to  that in the video description thank you  for watching i really appreciate your  time  i wish you the very best have a good  evening all the best to you and see you  next saturday

